<article class="env-lemma" id="0DXJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DXJ">Lemma <span data-tag="0DXJ">52.5.4</span>.</a> Let $(A, \mathfrak m)$ be a Noetherian local ring. Let $I \subset A$ be an ideal. Let $M$ be a finite $A$-module. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  H^ i(R\Gamma _\mathfrak m(M)^\wedge ) = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits H^ i_\mathfrak m(M/I^ nM)  \]
</div>
  <p> for all $i$ where $R\Gamma _\mathfrak m(M)^\wedge $ denotes the derived $I$-adic completion. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Dualizing Complexes, Lemma <a href="/tag/0EEW" data-tag="0EEW">47.12.4</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/0DX1" data-tag="0DX1">52.5.2</a> to see the vanishing of the $R^1\mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits $ terms. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>